// ================================================================
// UNIT SCHEMA CANONS - Core Meta-Schema Components
// ================================================================

Canon {
  name = comp_component
  category = meta_schema
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Defines a class or entity with name, parent, and searchability. The foundational building block of the unit schema system."
  doc = ~~~
Comp defines the structure of data types in the system. Each Comp has:
- A unique name identifying the component type
- A parent component (or '.' for top-level)
- A find mode controlling how instances are located
- Optional documentation

Find modes:
- Find: Top-level components searchable by name or key
- FindIn: Nested components searchable within parent context
- '.': No indexing, not directly searchable
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_element
  category = meta_schema
  topic_type = field_definition
  overview = "Defines a field within a component, specifying its name, type, linkage, validation rules, and documentation."
  doc = ~~~
Element defines individual fields within a Comp. Each Element has:
- A name identifying the field
- A type determining storage and behavior
- A comp reference for ref types
- A check constraint for validation
- Optional documentation

Elements are the data-carrying members of components.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_opt
  category = meta_schema
  topic_type = enumeration_value
  overview = "Defines allowable values for an element, adding semantic meaning and documentation to enumerated options."
  doc = ~~~
Opt provides named options for elements, typically used with 'word' type fields.
Each Opt represents one valid value with optional documentation explaining its meaning.

Opts create type-safe enumerations within the schema.
~~~
}

// ================================================================
// ELEMENT TYPE SYSTEM CANONS
// ================================================================

Canon {
  name = element_type_key
  category = element_type
  topic_type = data_type
  overview = "Primary index field for finding and uniquely identifying component instances."
  doc = "Key type elements serve as the unique identifier for Find/FindIn components. Used for lookups and references."
}

Canon {
  name = element_type_word
  category = element_type
  topic_type = data_type
  overview = "Single word value, typically used for enumerations, flags, or short identifiers."
  doc = "Word type elements store a single token without spaces. Often paired with Opt definitions for type-safe enumerations."
}

Canon {
  name = element_type_text
  category = element_type
  topic_type = data_type
  overview = "String extending to end of line, used for descriptions, documentation, or multi-word content."
  doc = "Text type elements capture all remaining content on a line, supporting spaces and longer-form text."
}

Canon {
  name = element_type_number
  category = element_type
  topic_type = data_type
  overview = "Numeric value supporting both storage and ordering operations."
  doc = "Number type elements store numeric data and can be used for sorting, indexing, and calculations."
}

Canon {
  name = element_type_tree
  category = element_type
  topic_type = data_type
  overview = "Numeric value enabling hierarchical tree navigation and depth tracking."
  doc = "Tree type elements store depth or level information, enabling parent-child tree traversal operations."
}

Canon {
  name = element_type_ref
  category = element_type
  topic_type = reference_type
  overview = "Direct reference to a top-level Find component instance by its key."
  doc = "Ref type elements create hard references to other components. The comp field specifies the target component type."
}

Canon {
  name = element_type_link
  category = element_type
  topic_type = reference_type
  overview = "Reference to a sibling component within the same parent context."
  doc = "Link type elements reference other instances at the same level in the hierarchy, enabling peer relationships."
}

Canon {
  name = element_type_type_of
  category = element_type
  topic_type = reference_type
  overview = "Reference by type name to a child component of a specific type."
  doc = "Type_of elements enable polymorphic references, selecting child components based on their type."
}

Canon {
  name = element_type_up_copy
  category = element_type
  topic_type = derived_reference
  overview = "Copies component ID from parent chain upward for use by subsequent ref_copy or ref_child elements."
  doc = "Up_copy walks up the parent hierarchy to capture an ID, setting context for derived references that follow."
}

Canon {
  name = element_type_ref_copy
  category = element_type
  topic_type = derived_reference
  overview = "Derived reference copying the reference value from the previous ref/link element's field."
  doc = "Ref_copy elements automatically populate by copying a reference from an earlier element in the same component."
}

Canon {
  name = element_type_ref_child
  category = element_type
  topic_type = derived_reference
  overview = "Derived reference looking up child components within the target of the previous element."
  doc = "Ref_child elements navigate into the component referenced by the prior element, accessing its children."
}

// ================================================================
// ELEMENT CHECK CONSTRAINT CANONS
// ================================================================

Canon {
  name = element_check_dot
  category = element_check
  topic_type = validation_rule
  overview = "Error if target not found when target is not dot (.)."
  doc = "Dot check enforces reference validity unless the target is explicitly '.' (null/none)."
}

Canon {
  name = element_check_plus
  category = element_check
  topic_type = validation_rule
  overview = "Error if target not found or if word field is empty (end of line)."
  doc = "Plus check mandates the presence of either a valid reference target or a non-empty word value."
}

Canon {
  name = element_check_one
  category = element_check
  topic_type = validation_rule
  overview = "Error if target not found OR if multiple targets found - enforces exactly one match."
  doc = "One check ensures singular reference resolution, rejecting both missing and ambiguous targets."
}

Canon {
  name = element_check_star
  category = element_check
  topic_type = validation_rule
  overview = "No error checking - target may be missing, word may be empty."
  doc = "Star check disables validation, allowing optional references and optional word values."
}

// ================================================================
// ELEMENT COMP TARGET CANONS
// ================================================================

Canon {
  name = element_comp_dot
  category = element_comp
  topic_type = reference_target
  overview = "Dot (.) as comp value indicates non-reference types or self-reference context."
  doc = "When comp is '.', the element is not a reference type (used for key, word, text, number, tree)."
}

Canon {
  name = element_comp_typed
  category = element_comp
  topic_type = reference_target
  overview = "Comp field specifies the target component type for ref/link/type_of/up_copy/ref_copy/ref_child elements."
  doc = "For reference types, comp names the Comp that this element points to, enabling type-safe linking."
}

// ================================================================
// ACTOR SYSTEM CANONS
// ================================================================

Canon {
  name = comp_actor
  category = code_generation
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Base type for code generator actors - routines that transform component definitions into executable code."
  doc = ~~~
Actor is the base component for all code generation directives. Actors are grouped by name and 
invoked by the generator to produce source code, documentation, or other artifacts.

Actors check conditions (comp, attr, eq, value) to determine when to execute.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_all
  category = actor_type
  topic_type = iteration_actor
  overview = "Actor that iterates over all components of a specified type, invoking another actor for each."
  doc = ~~~
All actor implements for-each iteration over components. For each component matching 'what',
it calls the referenced 'actor' with optional 'args'.

Used for generating repetitive code structures across multiple components.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_du
  category = actor_type
  topic_type = conditional_actor
  overview = "Conditional actor that invokes another actor based on condition evaluation."
  doc = "Du actor provides if-then logic, calling its referenced actor only when conditions are met."
}

Canon {
  name = comp_new
  category = actor_type
  topic_type = instantiation_actor
  overview = "Creates and adds new component instances during code generation."
  doc = ~~~
New actor dynamically instantiates components, either in data structures (dats) or actor 
definitions (acts), using provided line arguments.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_refs
  category = actor_type
  topic_type = validation_actor
  overview = "Re-runs reference resolution after loading new definitions."
  doc = "Refs actor triggers reference validation passes, ensuring all ref/link elements resolve correctly after schema changes."
}

Canon {
  name = comp_var
  category = actor_type
  topic_type = state_actor
  overview = "Sets generator variable to specified value for use in subsequent actors."
  doc = "Var actor manages generator state, storing values in named variables accessible by later code generation steps."
}

Canon {
  name = comp_its
  category = actor_type
  topic_type = traversal_actor
  overview = "Invokes actor for each child or reference of current component definition."
  doc = ~~~
Its actor traverses component relationships, calling an actor for each child component or 
reference relationship. Used for hierarchical code generation.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_c
  category = actor_type
  topic_type = output_actor
  overview = "Outputs code line to generated file with automatic newline."
  doc = "C actor emits a complete line of code to the output stream, the primary mechanism for code generation."
}

Canon {
  name = comp_cs
  category = actor_type
  topic_type = output_actor
  overview = "Outputs code snippet without newline, for inline code construction."
  doc = "Cs actor emits code fragments without line breaks, enabling multi-part line assembly."
}

Canon {
  name = comp_out
  category = actor_type
  topic_type = control_actor
  overview = "Controls output state: delay, normal, off, or on modes with optional padding and buffering."
  doc = ~~~
Out actor manages code generation output state:
- delay: suppress output until next C actor
- normal: restore default output behavior
- off: disable all output
- on: enable output

Supports padding and description buffering for formatted output.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_in
  category = actor_type
  topic_type = control_actor
  overview = "Redirects output to the 'ins' variable instead of file stream."
  doc = "In actor captures generated code into a variable for later use or processing, enabling multi-pass generation."
}

Canon {
  name = comp_break
  category = actor_type
  topic_type = control_flow_actor
  overview = "Breaks out of actor loops or command chains to control execution flow."
  doc = ~~~
Break actor provides loop and execution control:
- actor: continue with calling actor (break actor case)
- loop: continue after All/Its (break loop chain)
- cmds: continue with actor case (break command list)
- exit: terminate script

Optional 'check' field restricts break to non-unique cases only.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_add
  category = actor_type
  topic_type = collection_actor
  overview = "Adds items to collections (maps/lists) with options for nodes, JSON, files, URLs, and database queries."
  doc = ~~~
Add actor manages collection manipulation:
- Supports string data, nodes, JSON, maps, lists
- Can clear collections
- Can check for duplicates
- Can break on duplicates
- Supports file input, eval, HTTP, and SQL data sources

Path navigation uses '_.' for collection root and '.' for current node.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_this
  category = actor_type
  topic_type = traversal_actor
  overview = "Invokes actor for each child or item in a collection, supporting map/list navigation."
  doc = "This actor extends Its with collection support, iterating over map entries and list items in addition to component children."
}

Canon {
  name = comp_replace
  category = actor_type
  topic_type = string_actor
  overview = "String replacement with pattern matching, supporting grouped replacements."
  doc = "Replace actor performs pattern-based string substitution at specified node paths, with optional group capture support."
}

// ================================================================
// COGNITIVE DOMAIN CANONS
// ================================================================

Canon {
  name = comp_agent
  category = cognitive
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "The executing persona with identity, capabilities, and resource constraints."
  doc = ~~~
Agent represents an AI system instance with:
- Unique identity (agent_id)
- Persona definition (system prompt/role)
- Available tools and capabilities
- Token budget (context window limit)

Agents are the top-level actors in cognitive sessions.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_objective
  category = cognitive
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Goal structure with status, priority, and hierarchical sub-goal support."
  doc = ~~~
Objective represents goals and sub-goals:
- Hierarchical structure (parent_obj links)
- Status tracking (active, suspended, completed, failed, abandoned)
- Priority scoring (0.0-1.0)

Objectives organize agent work and track progress.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_memory
  category = cognitive
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Grounded knowledge store with type, source, confidence, and temporal tracking."
  doc = ~~~
Memory stores validated knowledge:
- Type: semantic, episodic, working, tool_result, meta
- Source: user, web, self, tool, training
- Confidence: 0.0-1.0 reliability score
- Timestamp: when created
- Optional embedding for semantic retrieval
- Invalidation tracking

Memories are the knowledge foundation for reasoning.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_thought
  category = cognitive
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Reasoning node in chain-of-thought or tree-of-thought structures with type and confidence."
  doc = ~~~
Thought represents reasoning steps:
- Type: reasoning, hypothesis, reflection, constraint, plan_step, synthesis, question, error_recovery
- Tree structure: level, prev (chain), branches (tree), parent_branch
- Confidence: 0.0-1.0 self-assessed certainty

Thoughts form the reasoning graph connecting objectives to conclusions.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_citation
  category = cognitive
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Explicit grounding link connecting thoughts to memory sources with role and optional quotes."
  doc = ~~~
Citation grounds thoughts in evidence:
- Links one Thought to one Memory (mandatory)
- Role: supports, contradicts, background, quote, evidence_for, evidence_against, invalidates
- Optional quote (max 15 words, copyright-safe)

Citations make reasoning transparent and verifiable.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_action
  category = cognitive
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "External execution request with tool, arguments, result tracking, and status."
  doc = ~~~
Action represents tool invocations:
- Tool reference (what capability)
- Arguments (JSON or code block)
- Result storage (result_mem)
- Status: pending, executing, success, error, timeout

Actions connect cognition to external capabilities.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_tool
  category = cognitive
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Available capability definition with name and schema specification."
  doc = "Tool defines agent capabilities, specifying function signatures or JSON schemas for invocation."
}

Canon {
  name = comp_vector
  category = cognitive
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Embedding representation for semantic search with dimensions and values."
  doc = "Vector stores high-dimensional embeddings for semantic similarity search over memories and knowledge."
}

// ================================================================
// SESSION MANAGEMENT CANONS
// ================================================================

Canon {
  name = comp_session
  category = session
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Container for cognitive work with agent, continuity chain, status, and timestamps."
  doc = ~~~
Session represents a complete cognitive work unit:
- Agent who performed the work
- Parent session for continuity
- Status: active, paused, completed, failed, abandoned
- Timestamp tracking

Sessions enable persistence and resumption of agent work.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_snapshot
  category = session
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Captures session state at a point in time with objectives, thoughts, and memories."
  doc = ~~~
Snapshot preserves session state:
- Trigger: manual, auto, error, milestone
- Captured objectives, thoughts, memories
- Timestamp

Snapshots enable checkpointing and rollback.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_restoration
  category = session
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Tracks what was loaded from previous sessions with source and relevance."
  doc = ~~~
Restoration documents session continuity:
- Source session and memory
- New memory created in current session
- Relevance score (0.0-1.0)

Restorations make session continuity explicit and traceable.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_crossref
  category = session
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Bidirectional linking between cognitive components and external systems."
  doc = ~~~
CrossRef connects cognitive and external domains:
- Cognitive component (type + ID)
- External component (type + ID)
- Relationship: generates, validates, executes, measures, invalidates, references
- Confidence: 0.0-1.0

CrossRefs enable validation and integration with external systems.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_cycle
  category = session
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Tracks learning through iteration with hypothesis, baseline, intervention, and outcome."
  doc = ~~~
Cycle documents learning loops:
- Trigger: error, optimization, requirement, feedback, exploration
- Hypothesis being tested
- Baseline state
- Intervention (what changed)
- Outcome (measured result)
- Improvement (quantified delta)

Cycles enable empirical learning and schema evolution.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_pattern
  category = session
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Extracted reusable knowledge with category, evidence, confidence, and applicability."
  doc = ~~~
Pattern captures generalizable insights:
- Category: bug_fix, optimization, design, constraint, heuristic
- Evidence from learning cycles
- Confidence: 0.0-1.0
- Applicability conditions

Patterns enable knowledge transfer across sessions.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_evolution
  category = session
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Tracks schema and domain changes over time with motivation and driving sessions."
  doc = ~~~
Evolution documents schema changes:
- Target schema (cog, session, omni, etc.)
- Change type: add_component, add_element, add_opt, deprecate, rename
- Motivation from patterns
- Driving sessions

Evolution makes schema development explicit and traceable.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_metric
  category = session
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Quantitative performance tracking with measurement method, value, and target."
  doc = "Metric captures measurable aspects of session performance, enabling data-driven optimization."
}

Canon {
  name = comp_artifact
  category = session
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "External files or data produced or consumed by sessions with type, format, and role."
  doc = ~~~
Artifact tracks external resources:
- Type: file, url, database, stream
- Format: json, rio, py, cu, md, etc.
- Role: input, output, intermediate, reference
- Size, hash, timestamp

Artifacts link sessions to their external products and dependencies.
~~~
}

// ================================================================
// CANON SYSTEM CANONS
// ================================================================

Canon {
  name = comp_canon
  category = canon_system
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Self-contained authoritative knowledge unit optimized for AI consumption with 10-30 line scope."
  doc = ~~~
Canon defines foundational knowledge:
- Unique name (key identifier)
- Category and topic_type for organization
- Overview: 1-3 sentence summary
- Doc: detailed explanation

Canons are the authoritative source, overruling derived schemas during bootstrap and recovery.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_link
  category = canon_system
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Typed relationship creating validated knowledge graph between Canons."
  doc = ~~~
Link creates semantic relationships:
- Concept: target Canon
- Relation: relationship type Canon

Links must reference existing Canons, creating a validated knowledge graph.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_section
  category = canon_system
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Optional structure for longer Canons with name, level, title, and markdown content."
  doc = ~~~
Section provides structure within Canons:
- Name: section identifier
- Level: heading depth (2=h2, 3=h3, 4=h4)
- Title: section heading
- Content: markdown body

Sections organize longer canonical documents.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_canonmeta
  category = canon_system
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Runtime metadata for Canons: executable status, maturity, usage count, and effectiveness."
  doc = ~~~
CanonMeta tracks Canon lifecycle:
- Executable: yes, no, partial
- Maturity: draft, stable, deprecated
- Usage count: implementation frequency
- Avg effectiveness: measured performance

CanonMeta enables data-driven Canon curation.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_implementation
  category = canon_system
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Records when a Canon gets instantiated in cognitive runtime with fidelity and effectiveness tracking."
  doc = ~~~
Implementation bridges Canon and execution:
- Canon being implemented
- Cognitive type and ID
- Session context
- Effectiveness: 0.0-1.0 outcome
- Adherence: 0.0-1.0 fidelity to Canon

Implementations provide empirical feedback on canonical knowledge.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_thoughtsource
  category = canon_system
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Links Thought components back to source Canon and Implementation."
  doc = "ThoughtSource makes thought provenance explicit, connecting reasoning steps to authoritative documentation."
}

Canon {
  name = comp_memorysource
  category = canon_system
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Links Memory components back to source Canon and Implementation."
  doc = "MemorySource grounds memories in canonical knowledge, enabling validation and evolution."
}

Canon {
  name = comp_patternsource
  category = canon_system
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Links Pattern components back to source Canon and all Implementations."
  doc = "PatternSource connects extracted patterns to their canonical origins and empirical evidence."
}

Canon {
  name = comp_canonversion
  category = canon_system
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Tracks Canon evolution with version chain, change type, motivation, and improvement metrics."
  doc = ~~~
CanonVersion documents Canon refinement:
- Version identifier
- Previous version link (chain)
- Change type: clarification, bugfix, enhancement, refactor
- Motivation and evidence
- Measured improvement

Versions enable empirical Canon evolution while preserving history.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_canoncycle
  category = canon_system
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Specialized learning cycle tracking Canon-driven improvement with baseline, issues, and resulting version."
  doc = ~~~
CanonCycle links empirical evidence to Canon evolution:
- Baseline Canon version
- Implementation instances
- Discovered issues
- Proposed changes
- New version

CanonCycles make documentation improvement systematic and data-driven.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_library
  category = canon_system
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Curated collection of Canons organized by domain and purpose for session loading or dynamic query."
  doc = ~~~
Library organizes Canons:
- Domain: reasoning, memory, planning, debugging, etc.
- Purpose: what this collection supports
- Canons: member canonical documents
- Maintainer and version

Libraries enable modular knowledge management.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_recommendation
  category = canon_system
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "AI-suggested Canon based on current context with confidence, reasoning, and outcome tracking."
  doc = ~~~
Recommendation captures intelligent suggestions:
- Situation: pattern match triggering suggestion
- Canon: recommended documentation
- Confidence: 0.0-1.0 recommendation strength
- Reasoning: why this Canon fits
- Accepted: yes, no, modified
- Outcome and implementation

Recommendations enable context-aware knowledge application.
~~~
}
